# Copy to `app/api/.env` (or the repo root) and fill in. Git-ignored.
# Loaded by `agents/__init__.py` at import, so every entry point sees it:
# the API background task, explorer.crawler, probe.py and smoke_run.py.
# An exported variable always wins over this file.

# One of these is strongly recommended. Without any, a run still
# produces a map -- `explorer.crawler` builds it breadth-first -- but it
# finishes `degraded`: no flows, no summary, and the intent is ignored.
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is probed first, on cost: a colony run is ~78 model
# calls, measured at $0.089 on qwen3-coder-next against ~$3.42 on
# claude-opus-5. Set OPENROUTER_MODEL to use a different model, or
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL to point the same code at DeepSeek, Groq, Cerebras
# or a local Ollama -- they all speak chat-completions.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-coder-next
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# When a key runs dry. OpenRouter checks `max_tokens` against the key's
# remaining budget *before* the model runs, so a nearly-empty key 402s a large
# request outright -- "requested up to 32768 tokens, but can only afford 268"
# -- and the account balance is not what it checks: a per-key spend cap binds
# first. Two ways out, and they trade different things:
#
#   LLM_MAX_TOKENS   shrinks every reply to fit. Truncates long `finish` calls.
#   LLM_FREE_FALLBACK=1  retries the 402 on the provider's `:free` route, which
#                    reserves nothing. Name a route instead of `1` to pick one.
#
# The fallback is OFF by default on purpose: a run that quietly finishes on a
# different model than it started on invalidates every comparison in
# docs/product/bets.md. When it fires it says so at `warn`, naming both routes.
# LLM_MAX_TOKENS=
# LLM_FREE_FALLBACK=

# Optional: what the form-filler types into sign-in fields it meets.
# AIVAR_USERNAME=
# AIVAR_PASSWORD=
